# Playwright QA Assessment Rules

## Scope

- SUT: https://practicesoftwaretesting.com (UI) and https://api.practicesoftwaretesting.com (API)
- Max 5–8 test cases per tier: manual, UI automation, API automation
- AC1: Registration/login/profile (UI) and auth/cart (API)
- AC2: Products/cart/checkout/invoice (UI) and products/cart/invoice (API)

## Tags

Use Playwright grep tags on every spec title:

- `@smoke` — critical path
- `@regression` — full AC coverage + negatives
- `@ui` or `@api` — project marker

Example: `test('TC-UI-02 should login @smoke @regression @ui', ...)`

## Test design

- UI: Page Object Model in `pages/`; no raw locators in specs when a page exists
- API: Service classes in `api/endpoints/`; use `fixtures/api.fixture.js`
- Prefer dynamic users (`data-generator.js`, API register) over shared demo account (lockout risk)
- UI checkout: Cash on Delivery requires **two Confirm clicks**; wait between payment check and invoice

## Execution

- UI runs on Chromium only (`ui-chromium` project)
- Local default: 1 worker for UI stability
- Reports: `reports/html`, `reports/json`, `reports/junit` (gitignored)
- Committed evidence: `PrismStructure/execution-report.md`

## Do not

- Add dependencies without justification
- Hardcode credentials in code or CSV
- Paste secrets into AI prompts or docs
